# ifvalue — `branch ifValue X <cmp> Y goto L` comparison sugar (README ss13).
# Prints "equal" because 5 equals 5. (todos WS1-066)

IfValue is project
IfValue module examplesIfValue
IfValue target console
IfValue entry main

examplesIfValue is module
examplesIfValue path examples.ifValue
examplesIfValue exports main
examplesIfValue purpose "Branch on a value comparison with ifValue"
examplesIfValue invariant "Reaches the equal path only when the operands compare equal"

ExitCode is alias
ExitCode for Int32
ExitCode purpose "Process exit status"

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout
stdoutWriter purpose "Allow controlled writes to standard output"

main is operation
main out ExitCode
main effect write console.stdout
main uses stdoutWriter
main memory heap no
main async no
main purpose "Compare two values with ifValue and print which path is taken"
main invariant "Prints equal iff the two operands compare equal"
main let left immutable Int64 5
main let right immutable Int64 5
main let equalText immutable String "equal"
main let differentText immutable String "different"
main let okCode immutable ExitCode 0
main branch ifValue left equals right goto bothEqual
main do writeDifferent
main return okCode
main at bothEqual do writeEqual
main return okCode

writeEqual is call
writeEqual in main
writeEqual invokes console.writeLine
writeEqual arg text String equalText

writeDifferent is call
writeDifferent in main
writeDifferent invokes console.writeLine
writeDifferent arg text String differentText
